@startuml
title Supplier Selection Multi-Agent System - Sequence Diagram

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 18
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor "Factory User" as FactoryUser
participant "Buyer Agent" as BuyerAgent
participant "Supplier Analysis Agent" as AnalysisAgent
participant "Supplier Information Tool" as SupplierTool

FactoryUser -> BuyerAgent : Submit factory request
BuyerAgent -> BuyerAgent : Identify decision criteria\nquantity, deadline, and user priority
BuyerAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Send request and criteria

AnalysisAgent -> SupplierTool : Request supplier information
SupplierTool --> AnalysisAgent : Return structured supplier facts

AnalysisAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Parse requested quantity and deadline
AnalysisAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Check hard constraints\ncapacity >= quantity\ndelivery <= deadline
AnalysisAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Compare feasible suppliers\nprice, delivery, reliability, and capacity
AnalysisAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Apply explicit user priority\nfor example, lowest cost

alt One or more suppliers are feasible
  AnalysisAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Select the best feasible supplier
else No supplier is feasible
  AnalysisAgent -> AnalysisAgent : Return "No feasible supplier"
end

note right of AnalysisAgent
  Local Ollama (qwen2.5:1.5b) remains in the workflow.
  Deterministic validation protects numeric constraints
  and supplier facts if the model response differs.
end note

AnalysisAgent --> BuyerAgent : Return recommendation and explanation
BuyerAgent -> BuyerAgent : Check risks and prepare final response
BuyerAgent --> FactoryUser : Return supplier recommendation

@enduml
